    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0184" n="116" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg116"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2021.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 18, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 6th of July, No. 1402. I thank you for the interesting account
                    you have given me of the demonstrations of official and popular feeling produced
                    by the; late tragical events in Mexico.</p>
                <p>You will easily infer the present attitude of this government towards Mexico from
                    a memorandum<anchor n="*" xml:id="d108-f1"/> made at this department on the 12th
                    instant, in regard to the adventures of Señor Santa Anna at Vera Cruz and Sisal,
                    a copy of which memorandum is herewith transmitted for your information.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d108-f1" n="*" xml:id="d108-f1-content">
                <p>For enclosure see instructions to United States minister to Mexico.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
